#: lib/mythweaver_web/live/ai_model_live.ex
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "\"Don't repeat yourself\": penalizes a token that would extend a phrase already in the context, growing with the phrase's length. The strongest cure for loops on local models; 0 turns it off, 0.8 is a common start. llama.cpp and TabbyAPI."
msgstr ""

#: lib/mythweaver_web/live/ai_model_live.ex
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "\"Exclude top choices\": when several tokens are at least this likely, all but the least likely of them are removed, steering away from the most predictable wording. 0.1 is a common start. llama.cpp and TabbyAPI."
msgstr ""

#. %{chat}, %{text_completion}, %{embedding} and %{classifier} are the mode option names in bold; %{chat_endpoint}, %{text_endpoint} and %{server_flags} are code.
#: lib/mythweaver_web/live/ai_model_live.ex
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "%{chat} sends the prompt as role-tagged messages to %{chat_endpoint}, and the backend applies the model's chat template. %{text_completion} sends one flat prompt to %{text_endpoint}, for base models or a template written into the prompt itself. %{embedding} turns text into vectors for Vector lore entries; it can't reply in chats. %{classifier} is a GoEmotions sequence classifier served like an embedding model (llama-server %{server_flags}), for the Expressions classifier setting; it can't reply in chats either. A model switches modes only while nothing uses it in a way the new mode can't serve."
msgstr ""

